  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246252/assets/e595bc1d2c4998c19d1e878bf04856cabb3eef94e665e527449ded66eded6ef1.png)\n\n- Translate it by $4$ units to the right to get the graph of $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-4).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246252/assets/4b5e2469ce9b19817f67b95a0ac0b402a3d5dec6db92b79f7c7e18331ef267af.png)",
